IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uro-nouns`

-- Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2026 (S.I. 2026/148): SCHEDULE 1.
-- Layer 1. Schedule 1 sets out Parts I, III, IV and V of Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act
-- 1992 as article 3 amends them. Every figure is stated by the Order, so every figure is a value. The Order
-- prints only the rows it states: Part I has items 2, 2A and 5; Part III has 1, 2, 3, 4, 7 and 8; Part IV has 1A,
-- 2 and 8; Part V has 1 to 12 but item 10 starts at (b). Rows the text does not print are not invented
-- (NOTES.md, fork F-07); asking for one is a "not covered" NOTHING.
-- Money is in pounds. A weekly rate where the Schedule says "the appropriate rate being determined in
-- accordance with section 65(3)" (or 69(1)) is chosen by the beneficiary's circumstances, which the Act decides
-- outside the text: the row (higher/lower/middle) is the input.

§ `Schedule 1 -- Provisions of Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act as amended by this Order`

§§ `Part I -- Contributory periodical benefits`

-- ruler:                                                                  weekly rate, pounds
-- src:460 | Schedule 1 — PROVISIONS OF SCHEDULE 4 TO THE CONTRIBUTIONS AND BENEFITS ACT AS AMENDED BY THIS ORDER
-- src:461 | Part I — CONTRIBUTORY PERIODICAL BENEFITS
-- src:462 | | Description of benefit | Weekly rate |
-- src:463 | | 2. | Short-term incapacity benefit. | (a) lower rate | £110.70 |
-- src:464 | | | (b) higher rate | £130.90 |
-- src:465 | | 2A. | Long-term incapacity benefit. | | £146.60 |
-- src:466 | | 5. | Category B retirement pension where section 48A(4) or 48AA(4) applies. | | £110.75 |
@ref Sch 1 Part I (src:460-466)
DECLARE `a weekly rate in Part I of Schedule 4` IS ONE OF
    `short-term incapacity benefit, lower rate`
    `short-term incapacity benefit, higher rate`
    `long-term incapacity benefit`
    `Category B retirement pension where section 48A(4) or 48AA(4) applies`

@ref Sch 1 Part I (src:460-466)
GIVEN `which rate` IS A `a weekly rate in Part I of Schedule 4`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 Part I: the weekly rate` `which rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which rate`
    WHEN `short-term incapacity benefit, lower rate`                                 THEN 110.70   -- item 2(a)
    WHEN `short-term incapacity benefit, higher rate`                                THEN 130.90   -- item 2(b)
    WHEN `long-term incapacity benefit`                                              THEN 146.60   -- item 2A
    WHEN `Category B retirement pension where section 48A(4) or 48AA(4) applies`     THEN 110.75   -- item 5

§§ `Part III -- Non-contributory periodical benefits`

-- ruler:                                                    weekly rate, pounds
-- src:467 | Part III — NON-CONTRIBUTORY PERIODICAL BENEFITS
-- src:468 | | Description of benefit | Weekly rate |
-- src:469 | | 1. | Attendance allowance. | (a) higher rate | £114.60 |
-- src:470 | | | | (b) lower rate | £76.70 |
-- src:471 | | | | (the appropriate rate being determined in accordance with section 65(3)). |
-- src:472 | | 2. | Severe disablement allowance. | | £103.85 |
-- src:473 | | 3. | Age related addition. | (a) higher rate | £15.50 |
-- src:474 | | | | (b) middle rate | £8.60 |
-- src:475 | | | | (c) lower rate | £8.60 |
-- src:476 | | | | (the appropriate rate being determined in accordance with section 69(1)). |
-- src:477 | | 4. | Carer’s allowance. | | £86.45 |
-- src:478 | | 7. | Category D retirement pension. | | £110.75 |
-- src:479 | | 8. | Age addition (to a pension of any category, and otherwise under section 79). | | £0.25. |
@ref Sch 1 Part III (src:467-479)
DECLARE `a weekly rate in Part III of Schedule 4` IS ONE OF
    `attendance allowance, higher rate`
    `attendance allowance, lower rate`
    `severe disablement allowance`
    `age related addition, higher rate`
    `age related addition, middle rate`
    `age related addition, lower rate`
    `carer's allowance`
    `Category D retirement pension`
    `age addition (to a pension of any category, and otherwise under section 79)`

@ref Sch 1 Part III (src:467-479)
GIVEN `which rate` IS A `a weekly rate in Part III of Schedule 4`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 Part III: the weekly rate` `which rate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which rate`
    WHEN `attendance allowance, higher rate`                                              THEN 114.60   -- item 1(a)
    WHEN `attendance allowance, lower rate`                                               THEN 76.70    -- item 1(b)
    WHEN `severe disablement allowance`                                                   THEN 103.85   -- item 2
    WHEN `age related addition, higher rate`                                              THEN 15.50    -- item 3(a)
    WHEN `age related addition, middle rate`                                              THEN 8.60     -- item 3(b)
    WHEN `age related addition, lower rate`                                               THEN 8.60     -- item 3(c)
    WHEN `carer's allowance`                                                              THEN 86.45    -- item 4
    WHEN `Category D retirement pension`                                                  THEN 110.75   -- item 7
    WHEN `age addition (to a pension of any category, and otherwise under section 79)`    THEN 0.25     -- item 8

§§ `Part IV -- Increases for dependants`

-- The adult dependant increase with short-term incapacity benefit turns on whether "the beneficiary is under
-- pensionable age" or "over pensionable age"; a beneficiary exactly AT pensionable age is in neither, and
-- gets NOTHING (fork F-04). "pensionable age" is defined outside the text.
-- src:480 | Part IV — INCREASES FOR DEPENDANTS
-- src:481 | | Benefit to which increase applies (1) | Increase for adult dependant (3) |
-- src:483 | | 1A. | Short-term incapacity benefit— | |
-- src:484 | | | (a) | where the beneficiary is under pensionable age; | 66.35 |
-- src:485 | | | (b) | where the beneficiary is over pensionable age. | 82.00 |
-- src:486 | | 2. | Long-term incapacity benefit. | 85.15 |
-- src:487 | | 8. | Severe disablement allowance. | 51.05 |
@ref Sch 1 Part IV (src:480-487)
DECLARE `a benefit with an increase for an adult dependant in Part IV` IS ONE OF
    `increase for an adult dependant with short-term incapacity benefit`
    `increase for an adult dependant with long-term incapacity benefit`
    `increase for an adult dependant with severe disablement allowance`

-- out of text: pensionable age (Pensions Act 1995 Sch 4 / Pensions Act 2014 definitions): whether the beneficiary is under, at or over it is an input.
@ref Sch 1 Part IV (src:480-487)
GIVEN `which benefit` IS A `a benefit with an increase for an adult dependant in Part IV`
      `the beneficiary's position relative to pensionable age` IS A `a position relative to pensionable age`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 1 Part IV: the increase for an adult dependant` `which benefit` `the beneficiary's position relative to pensionable age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which benefit`
    WHEN `increase for an adult dependant with short-term incapacity benefit` THEN
        CONSIDER `the beneficiary's position relative to pensionable age`
        WHEN `under pensionable age` THEN JUST 66.35   -- item 1A(a)
        WHEN `over pensionable age` THEN JUST 82.00    -- item 1A(b)
        WHEN `at pensionable age` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `increase for an adult dependant with long-term incapacity benefit` THEN JUST 85.15   -- item 2
    WHEN `increase for an adult dependant with severe disablement allowance` THEN JUST 51.05   -- item 8

§§ `Part V -- Rates of industrial injuries benefit`

-- item 1. Degrees of disablement not in column (1) are not in the table: NOTHING (fork F-07).
-- src:488 | Part V — RATES OF INDUSTRIAL INJURIES BENEFIT
-- src:489 | | Description of benefit, etc. | Rate |
-- src:490 | | 1. | Disablement pension (weekly rates). | For the several degrees of disablement set out in column (1) of the following Table, the respective amounts in column (2) of that Table. |
-- src:491 | | | | | TABLE |
-- src:492 | | | | Degree of Disablement | Amount |
-- src:493 | | | | (1) | (2) | |
-- src:494 | | | | Per cent. | £ | |
-- src:495 | | | | 100 | 233.90 | |
-- src:496 | | | | 90 | 210.51 | |
-- src:497 | | | | 80 | 187.12 | |
-- src:498 | | | | 70 | 163.73 | |
-- src:499 | | | | 60 | 140.34 | |
-- src:500 | | | | 50 | 116.95 | |
-- src:501 | | | | 40 | 93.56 | |
-- src:502 | | | | 30 | 70.17 | |
-- src:503 | | | | 20 | 46.78 | |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 1 (src:488-503)
GIVEN `the degree of disablement, per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 1 Part V item 1: the weekly rate of disablement pension for the degree of disablement` `the degree of disablement, per cent` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the degree of disablement, per cent`
    WHEN 100 THEN JUST 233.90
    WHEN 90  THEN JUST 210.51
    WHEN 80  THEN JUST 187.12
    WHEN 70  THEN JUST 163.73
    WHEN 60  THEN JUST 140.34
    WHEN 50  THEN JUST 116.95
    WHEN 40  THEN JUST 93.56
    WHEN 30  THEN JUST 70.17
    WHEN 20  THEN JUST 46.78
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- item 2. Two maxima: (a) applies "except in cases of exceptionally severe disablement"; (b) applies "in any
-- case". Where (a) applies, both apply and the lower (a) binds; where (a) does not apply, only (b) does.
-- src:504 | | 2. | Maximum increase of weekly rate of disablement pension where constant attendance needed. | (a) | except in cases of exceptionally severe disablement | £93.60; |
-- src:505 | | | | (b) | in any case | £187.20. |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 2(a) (src:504-505)
`Sch 1 Part V item 2(a): the maximum increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension where constant attendance is needed, except in cases of exceptionally severe disablement` MEANS 93.60

@ref Sch 1 Part V item 2(b) (src:505)
`Sch 1 Part V item 2(b): the maximum increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension where constant attendance is needed, in any case` MEANS 187.20

-- out of text: Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 Sch 7 (constant attendance; exceptionally severe disablement): whether the disablement is exceptionally severe is an input.
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 2 (src:504-505)
GIVEN `the disablement is exceptionally severe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 Part V item 2: the maximum increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension where constant attendance is needed` `the disablement is exceptionally severe` MEANS
    IF `the disablement is exceptionally severe`
    THEN `Sch 1 Part V item 2(b): the maximum increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension where constant attendance is needed, in any case`
    ELSE `Sch 1 Part V item 2(a): the maximum increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension where constant attendance is needed, except in cases of exceptionally severe disablement`

-- src:506 | | 3. | Increase of weekly rate of disablement pension (exceptionally severe disablement). | | | £93.60. |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 3 (src:506)
`Sch 1 Part V item 3: the increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension for exceptionally severe disablement` MEANS 93.60

-- src:507 | | 4. | Maximum of aggregate of weekly benefit payable for successive accidents. | | | £233.90. |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 4 (src:507)
`Sch 1 Part V item 4: the maximum of the aggregate of weekly benefit payable for successive accidents` MEANS 233.90

-- src:508 | | 5. | Unemployability supplement under paragraph 2 of Schedule 7. | | | £144.65. |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 5 (src:508)
`Sch 1 Part V item 5: the unemployability supplement under paragraph 2 of Schedule 7` MEANS 144.65

-- out of text: Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 Sch 7 para 3 (qualifying date) and pensionable age: the age on the qualifying date, the qualifying date and whether pensionable age was attained before 6th April 1979 are inputs.
-- item 6. The heads are tried in order: "(b) if head (a) above does not apply", "(c) if heads (a) and (b) above
-- do not apply", and so on; a BRANCH takes the first arm that holds. "Pensionable age" is defined outside the text.
-- src:509 | | 6. | Increase under paragraph 3 of Schedule 7 of weekly rate of unemployability supplement. | (a) | if on the qualifying date the beneficiary was under the age of 35 or if that date fell before 5th July 1948 | £30.00 |
-- src:510 | | | | (b) | if head (a) above does not apply and on the qualifying date the beneficiary was under the age of 40 and he had not attained pensionable age before 6th April 1979 | £30.00 |
-- src:511 | | | | (c) | if heads (a) and (b) above do not apply and on the qualifying date the beneficiary was under the age of 45 | £19.20 |
-- src:512 | | | | (d) | if heads (a), (b) and (c) above do not apply and on the qualifying date the beneficiary was under the age of 50 and had not attained pensionable age before 6th April 1979 | £19.20 |
-- src:513 | | | | (e) | in any other case | £9.60. |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 6 (src:509-513)
GIVEN `the age of the beneficiary on the qualifying date` IS A NUMBER
      `the qualifying date fell before 5th July 1948` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficiary had attained pensionable age before 6th April 1979` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 Part V item 6: the increase of the weekly rate of unemployability supplement` `the age of the beneficiary on the qualifying date` `the qualifying date fell before 5th July 1948` `the beneficiary had attained pensionable age before 6th April 1979` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the age of the beneficiary on the qualifying date` LESS THAN 35 OR `the qualifying date fell before 5th July 1948`
        THEN 30.00   -- (a)
        IF `the age of the beneficiary on the qualifying date` LESS THAN 40 AND (NOT `the beneficiary had attained pensionable age before 6th April 1979`)
        THEN 30.00   -- (b)
        IF `the age of the beneficiary on the qualifying date` LESS THAN 45
        THEN 19.20   -- (c)
        IF `the age of the beneficiary on the qualifying date` LESS THAN 50 AND (NOT `the beneficiary had attained pensionable age before 6th April 1979`)
        THEN 19.20   -- (d)
        OTHERWISE 9.60   -- (e) in any other case

-- src:514 | | 7. | Increase under paragraph 4 of Schedule 7 of weekly rate of disablement pension. | | | £11.35. |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 7 (src:514)
`Sch 1 Part V item 7: the increase under paragraph 4 of Schedule 7 of the weekly rate of disablement pension` MEANS 11.35

-- src:515 | | 8. | Increase under paragraph 6 of Schedule 7 of weekly rate of disablement pension. | | | £86.45. |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 8 (src:515)
`Sch 1 Part V item 8: the increase under paragraph 6 of Schedule 7 of the weekly rate of disablement pension` MEANS 86.45

-- src:516 | | 9. | Maximum disablement gratuity under paragraph 9 of Schedule 7. | | | £15,520.00 |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 9 (src:516)
`Sch 1 Part V item 9: the maximum disablement gratuity under paragraph 9 of Schedule 7` MEANS 15520.00

-- src:517 | | 10. | Widow’s pension (weekly rates) . | (b) | higher permanent rate | £184.90; |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 10(b) (src:517)
`Sch 1 Part V item 10(b): the widow's pension at the higher permanent rate` MEANS 184.90

-- item 10(c): "30 per cent of the first sum specified in section 44(4)". The Order does not say which of the two sums
-- it substitutes in section 44(4) (art 4(2)(a), (b)) is "the first sum", so that sum is an input (fork F-05).
-- out of text: Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 s 44(4), the first sum
-- src:518 | | | | (c) | lower permanent rate 30 per cent of the first sum specified in section 44(4) (Category A basic retirement pension) (the appropriate rate being determined in accordance with paragraph 16 of Schedule 7) | |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 10(c) (src:518)
GIVEN `the first sum specified in section 44(4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 Part V item 10(c): the widow's pension at the lower permanent rate` `the first sum specified in section 44(4)` MEANS
    `the first sum specified in section 44(4)` TIMES 30%

-- src:519 | | 11. | Widower’s pension (weekly rate). | £184.90. |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 11 (src:519)
`Sch 1 Part V item 11: the widower's pension` MEANS 184.90

-- src:520 | | 12. | Weekly rate of allowance in respect of children and qualifying young persons under paragraph 18 of Schedule 7. | In respect of each child or qualifying young person | £11.35. |
@ref Sch 1 Part V item 12 (src:520)
`Sch 1 Part V item 12: the allowance in respect of each child or qualifying young person under paragraph 18 of Schedule 7` MEANS 11.35

DECLARE `a single-figure row of Part V of Schedule 4` IS ONE OF
    `the increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension for exceptionally severe disablement`
    `the maximum of the aggregate of weekly benefit payable for successive accidents`
    `the unemployability supplement`
    `the increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension under paragraph 4 of Schedule 7`
    `the increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension under paragraph 6 of Schedule 7`
    `the maximum disablement gratuity`
    `the widow's pension at the higher permanent rate`
    `the widower's pension`
    `the allowance in respect of each child or qualifying young person`

@ref Sch 1 Part V (src:488-520)
GIVEN `which row` IS A `a single-figure row of Part V of Schedule 4`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 1 Part V: the single figure` `which row` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which row`
    WHEN `the increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension for exceptionally severe disablement`   THEN `Sch 1 Part V item 3: the increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension for exceptionally severe disablement`
    WHEN `the maximum of the aggregate of weekly benefit payable for successive accidents`               THEN `Sch 1 Part V item 4: the maximum of the aggregate of weekly benefit payable for successive accidents`
    WHEN `the unemployability supplement`                                                                THEN `Sch 1 Part V item 5: the unemployability supplement under paragraph 2 of Schedule 7`
    WHEN `the increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension under paragraph 4 of Schedule 7`        THEN `Sch 1 Part V item 7: the increase under paragraph 4 of Schedule 7 of the weekly rate of disablement pension`
    WHEN `the increase of the weekly rate of disablement pension under paragraph 6 of Schedule 7`        THEN `Sch 1 Part V item 8: the increase under paragraph 6 of Schedule 7 of the weekly rate of disablement pension`
    WHEN `the maximum disablement gratuity`                                                              THEN `Sch 1 Part V item 9: the maximum disablement gratuity under paragraph 9 of Schedule 7`
    WHEN `the widow's pension at the higher permanent rate`                                              THEN `Sch 1 Part V item 10(b): the widow's pension at the higher permanent rate`
    WHEN `the widower's pension`                                                                         THEN `Sch 1 Part V item 11: the widower's pension`
    WHEN `the allowance in respect of each child or qualifying young person`                             THEN `Sch 1 Part V item 12: the allowance in respect of each child or qualifying young person under paragraph 18 of Schedule 7`
